# Cloudflare Pages header rules for hotline.dev (project: hotline-site).
# This file is parsed by Pages and is never served as an asset.
#
# `/install.sh` is a real file in this directory, so Pages matches it exactly and
# it is served ahead of the not-found fallback that turns every other unmatched
# path into index.html. That exact match is what keeps
# `curl hotline.dev/install.sh | sh` from ever piping HTML into a shell.
#
# The extension is deliberate: it says what the script is, and leaves the door
# open for an install.ps1 sibling without renaming the one people already have.
#
# Content-Type is pinned to text/plain so the URL is READABLE IN A BROWSER.
# Left alone, a shell script is typed as a download (or as application/x-sh,
# which browsers also download) — and the whole security argument for this
# installer is that you read it before you pipe it into a shell. Do not drop
# this header: curl does not care, people do.
#
# A future install.ps1 wants the same treatment — copy the block below:
#
#   /install.ps1
#     Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
#     Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
#     X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/install.sh
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
